  "data": {
    "accession": "PXD051261",
    "title": "AE-MS to profile SLO-human plasma protein interactome landscape; HDX-MS and XL-MS to study protein interaction and dynamics of PLG-SLO",
    "additionalAttributes": [],
    "projectDescription": "Group A Streptococcus is known to exploit the human fibrinolysis system, particularly by targeting the plasminogen/plasmin pathway through redundant pathomechanisms. In this study, we began with affinity-enrichment mass spectrometry to map the interaction landscape between streptolysin O and human plasma, identifying human plasminogen as a specific binder to the streptolysin O. Subsequent biochemical assays validated this direct interaction and demonstrated the streptolysin O's role in enhancing tPA-mediated plasmin production. We then employed HDX-MS and XL-MS to further explore and characterize the molecular details of the plasminogen-streptolysin O complex formation, shedding light on its biological significance.",
    "sampleProcessingProtocol": "i) Affinity-tag-fused SLO protein was designed, expressed, and purified along with other background baits. The pulled-down samples were precipitated and subjected to in-solution digestion as described in previous studies. The digested peptides were cleaned-up, dried, and reconstituted before being analyzed by mass spectrometry in both DIA and DDA modes. ii) In-solution cross-linking mass spectrometry was performed on plasminogen and streptolysin O proteins as previously described. A two-step digestion protocol was applied, and sample preparation was conducted as above. iii) Hydrogen/Deuterium exchange mass spectrometry was conducted on the plasminogen protein in both its apo and SLO-bound states. A pool of digested plasminogen peptides was determined by MS/MS, and MS1 scans were collected for HDX experiments.",
    "dataProcessingProtocol": "i) MaxQuant software was used for DIA and DDA identification/quantification in AE-MS datasets. ii) pLink 2, MaxLynx, and TX-MS (targeted cross-linking mass spectrometry) were utilized to analyze and search cross-linked peptide pairs. iii) HDExaminer and Deuteros 2.0 were used to analyze HDX-MS datasets.",
    "projectTags": [],
